diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..11493ee 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,32 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` in the
+server environment (see `.env.example`). The sender must be an SMS-capable Twilio
+number; trial accounts can send only to approved recipients. Without credentials,
+the form reports a delivery failure and never bypasses verification.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint sends six-digit codes, stores only salted
+code hashes in the server session, expires codes after five minutes, limits each
+code to five attempts, and enforces a 60-second send cooldown per session. A valid
+code is consumed before forwarding registration to the existing account API.
+Registration failures require a new code. The verified number is forwarded as
+`phoneNumber`; persistence depends on the external account service's schema.
+The external account API remains independently reachable, so enforcing phone
+verification for every account also requires that service to restrict direct
+registration or verify trusted server-side proof.
+
+Messages end in `@<request-hostname> #<code>` for origin-bound SMS extraction.
+Serve the page over HTTPS in production. WebOTP is feature-detected; keyboard
+autofill, paste, and manual input remain available when it is unsupported or denied.
+
+The Node adapter uses filesystem sessions by default. Production deployments with
+multiple instances need a shared persistent session driver and shared atomic
+rate/attempt limits. Apply provider spending limits and edge/IP/phone send limits
+before public deployment; the per-session cooldown alone does not prevent abuse
+from new sessions. Do not log codes, credentials, or phone numbers.
+
+Run the verification logic tests with `node --experimental-strip-types --test src/server/sms-verification.test.ts`.
